### JoisEyes PC service — plain-HTTP view of the current-state MCP tool
###
### GET /api/v1/current-state returns the exact same document as the
### `current-state` MCP tool (App\MCP\Tools\CurrentStateTool / App\Service\
### CurrentState\CurrentStateResolver) — the phone's entire /v1/snapshot
### body (every section — meta, power, screen, dnd, location, activity,
### environment, wearables, health_connect, connectivity, bt_devices),
### untouched, with our decorations added alongside the raw fields
### (server_time, verdict, location.place/source/note, screen.note,
### activity.intensity/in_motion, band.hr_age_relative, bt_devices[].label/
### note, ...). Nothing is chopped out or reshaped. Added 29.08.2026 so
### Stan can poll it directly, the same way he already polls the phone's
### own raw /v1/snapshot (see test_snapshot.http) — and see literally the
### same thing an agent sees via MCP.
###
### Under /api/v1/*, not /v1/* — deliberately a different namespace from
### the phone-sync contract routes (/v1/ingest, /v1/health, /v1/ping).
###
### This service runs on this same machine (see CLAUDE.md — port 9091, all
### interfaces), so no tailnet host/environment indirection is needed here,
### unlike test_snapshot.http's phone-on-the-tailnet setup.
###
### Always does one live read from the phone first (a real network call,
### same as test_snapshot.http's plain GET /v1/snapshot) — falls back to
### the last cached snapshot, then to stored records, only if the phone is
### unreachable. No force_steps/force_hr params anymore; every call is live.

### Default call.
GET http://localhost:9091/api/v1/current-state

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
    client.test("server_time is first and in Europe/Sofia", () => {
        const keys = Object.keys(response.body);
        client.assert(keys[0] === "server_time", `expected server_time first, got ${keys[0]}`);
        client.assert(response.body.server_time.timezone === "Europe/Sofia");
    });
    client.test("has our decoration keys alongside the raw snapshot", () => {
        const b = response.body;
        ["verdict", "last_activity", "looking_at_phone", "fallback"].forEach(key =>
            client.assert(key in b, `missing key: ${key}`)
        );
    });
    client.test("has the raw snapshot's sections too, not just decorations", () => {
        const b = response.body;
        ["meta", "power", "screen", "dnd", "location", "activity", "environment",
         "wearables", "health_connect", "connectivity", "bt_devices"].forEach(key =>
            client.assert(key in b, `missing raw section: ${key} — snapshot got chopped again`)
        );
    });
%}

### Unknown route — expect a normal Symfony 404, not this app's JSON shape.
GET http://localhost:9091/api/v1/nonexistent-route

> {%
    client.test("status is 404", () => client.assert(response.status === 404));
%}
